/.vscode/launch.json.bak

# Build artefacts of `npm run build:all`'s last two steps, both written to the repository root and both
# regenerable (`npm run docs:pdf`, `npm run package:dist`). The archives are ~24 MB each and are never
# overwritten — the name carries the build time — so without this rule a few builds would leave a
# hundred megabytes of untracked files in a tracked directory. NOT backup items either, for the same
# reason `dist/` is not: they are regenerated, and the markdown they come from IS backed up.
psss-engine-v2-distribution_*.zip
psss-engine-v2_how_it_works.pdf
psss-engine-v2_how_to_use_it.pdf
psss_research_v2.pdf

# The .NET screensaver host's build output, and the web bundle the build copies in beside its sources.
# `bin/` + `obj/` are ~133 MB and `bin/` also holds a duplicate of the `.scr` that `dist/screensaver/`
# already carries; `Payload/` is regenerated from `dist/` by `build:screensaver`, so committing it
# would ship the engine twice. All of it comes back from `npm run build:all`.
psss-engine/screensaver/bin/
psss-engine/screensaver/obj/
psss-engine/screensaver/Payload/

# The screensaver probe's captured screenshots — run artefacts beside PowerShell scripts that ARE
# source, which is why this is a file pattern and not the directory.
psss-engine/screensaver/probe/shot-*.png
psss-engine/screensaver/probe/_t.png

